@.str.310 = private unnamed_addr constant [2653 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Start a shell with the build environment of the default package of\0A  the flake in the current directory:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop\0A  ```\0A\0A  Typical commands to run inside this shell are:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # configurePhase\0A  # buildPhase\0A  # installPhase\0A  ```\0A\0A  Alternatively, you can run whatever build tools your project uses\0A  directly, e.g. for a typical Unix project:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # ./configure --prefix=$out\0A  # make\0A  # make install\0A  ```\0A\0A* Run a particular build phase directly:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop --unpack\0A  # nix develop --configure\0A  # nix develop --build\0A  # nix develop --check\0A  # nix develop --install\0A  # nix develop --installcheck\0A  ```\0A\0A* Start a shell with the build environment of GNU Hello:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop nixpkgs#hello\0A  ```\0A\0A* Record a build environment in a profile:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop --profile /tmp/my-build-env nixpkgs#hello\0A  ```\0A\0A* Use a build environment previously recorded in a profile:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop /tmp/my-build-env\0A  ```\0A\0A* Replace all occurrences of the store path corresponding to\0A  `glibc.dev` with a writable directory:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop --redirect nixpkgs#glibc.dev ~/my-glibc/outputs/dev\0A  ```\0A\0A  Note that this is useful if you're running a `nix develop` shell for\0A  `nixpkgs#glibc` in `~/my-glibc` and want to compile another package\0A  against it.\0A\0A* Run a series of script commands:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix develop --command bash -c \22mkdir build && cmake .. && make\22\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix develop` starts a `bash` shell that provides an interactive build\0Aenvironment nearly identical to what Nix would use to build\0A[*installable*](./nix.md#installables). Inside this shell, environment variables and shell\0Afunctions are set up so that you can interactively and incrementally\0Abuild your package.\0A\0ANix determines the build environment by building a modified version of\0Athe derivation *installable* that just records the environment\0Ainitialised by `stdenv` and exits. This build environment can be\0Arecorded into a profile using `--profile`.\0A\0AThe prompt used by the `bash` shell can be customised by setting the\0A`bash-prompt`, `bash-prompt-prefix`, and `bash-prompt-suffix` settings in\0A`nix.conf` or in the flake's `nixConfig` attribute.\0A\0A# Flake output attributes\0A\0AIf no flake output attribute is given, `nix develop` tries the following\0Aflake output attributes:\0A\0A* `devShells.<system>.default`\0A\0A* `packages.<system>.default`\0A\0AIf a flake output *name* is given, `nix develop` tries the following flake\0Aoutput attributes:\0A\0A* `devShells.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A* `packages.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A* `legacyPackages.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A\00", align 1
